{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision","id":1546428,"title":"Microscopic Vision","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-26T17:18:24-08:00","id":1546428,"title":"Microscopic Vision","content":"What would be involved in using magick to give oneself microscopic sight? I haven't been able to find an example of this in any of the source material available to me.<br /> <br /> This seems like it would fall under Correspondence, but all examples I've read involve shifting perceptions between locations, not altering the scale or focus of perception beyond innate capabilities.<br /> <br /> If a mage were to start looking at things on a sub-microscopic scale, that would probably involve a conjunctional effect based on the sort of thing you're looking at, as you're getting down to the nitty-gritty of quintessential patterns there (and how they perceive these things would depend upon their personal paradigm.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T01:07:18-08:00","id":1546443,"title":"","content":"I would say that would be life 1 (to get better eyesight). Corespondence could work on 4 where you can make things seem bigger than they are in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T01:39:30-08:00","id":1546444,"title":"","content":"Truly microscopic vision would be Forces 2: you're just altering light (or others if you want to get smaller) waves like you would a set of lenses. That's what microscopes do. They adjust light to see just a small bit of area and magnify it.<br /> <br /> Life 1/Matter 1 could be a form of microscopic vision for techno-magic oriented mages, but it's less &quot;see things like you would in a microscope&quot; and more &quot;how do filter detecting microscopic Patterns through that Focus.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T07:30:59-08:00","id":1546451,"title":"","content":"Perception effects can be skinned however is appropriate for the mage in question so as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> indicated, you have to distinguish between the effect &quot;manipulate the world to see things as if through a microscope&quot; and &quot;theme the perception effect as microscopic vision.&quot;<br /> <br /> A spell that actually works like a microscope is going to be a Forces 2 effect to manipulate the light, Life 3/4 to physically change the structure of the eye, or maybe Correspondence 3 to colocate perceptions in a clever way.<br /> <br /> A spell that is themed like a microscope is much more open and could include the Life 1/Matter 1 option. Correspondence 1 in theory should show everything in the area though I'm inclined to say that method will definitely need the Mind 1 option of processing multiple inputs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T15:02:23-08:00","id":1546458,"title":"","content":"Where to assign things if trying with Life is... complicated. And frankly it ends up as one of those things that feels like it should be lower level and quite simple, but by the ways the rules are written is actually the opposite. You're not just giving yourself another animal's features, you're giving yourself something that doesn't actually exist in natural living creatures.<br /> <br /> So, you're going to have to decide for your table if the game is more fun not being terribly strict in interpreting the rules, or if the game is more fun when the rules have greater consistence even if that means certain effects feel far harder than it seems worth pursuing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T16:00:30-08:00","id":1546460,"title":"","content":"These are all really good points!<br /> <br /> I hadn't considered using a Forces effect to focus reflected light in order to provide a very close-up view of an object, but I see no reason why it wouldn't work, so long as it falls within the paradigm of the mage attempting it. Probably most conceptualizations of the nature of light would allow it, unless you're talking about settings in very early history. This is probably one of those uses of Forces which would require a certain amount of practice. beyond just understanding the basic idea, (I can see some damage being done to one's own eyes without a good feel for exactly what you're doing here.)<br /> <br /> Enhancing one's own eyes to allow this sort of magnification would be the more difficult approach, magickally speaking, but I can see Progenitors (and some Etherites) with the required skill favoring this option. (Granted, either would probably prefer to use an actual microscope, but one doesn't always have one handy in the field.)<br /> <br /> I would probably let someone do this with a Correspondence 2 effect, provided it falls into line with their own practices of magic. If a mage uses a telescope as a tool for Correspondence, for instance, the idea of exploiting the same concept &quot;in reverse&quot; seems fairly natural to me. A Virtual Adept who understands the world as a manifestation of information could probably justify filtering that to a much smaller scale for examination. To a Hermetic, it might simply be a matter of adjusting mathematics and symbols they use to provide this sort of focus, when making use of scrying practices.<br /> <br /> When attempting to view things at molecular scales or lower, I would require an appropriate conjunctional pattern sensing effect, as that's getting down to the underling nature of things, and those subscribing to different paradigms are going to perceive these things differently. As brilliant as Epicurious and Lucretius were, and I'm convinced either or both were probably mages in the World of Darkness, not all paradigms take an atomist view of reality beyond a &quot;practical&quot; level. A Progenitor or Etherite might see DNA within a person's cells, but a Verbena or Dreamspeaker is likely to see a Life pattern represented quite differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 11-27-2024, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T18:26:04-08:00","id":1546462,"title":"","content":"If one works in fields where microscopy is common, it's a lot easier to have one on you than it used to be. Portable digital microscopes are pretty decent (at least equal to any standard compound microscope you'd find in most university non-specialty labs), and these days can Bluetooth right to your smartphone or laptop which helps a lot in portability because you cut out a lot of mass that way. Given what's commercially available, a Technocrat that does any sort of field work in biology/etc. would probably have a microscope in their kit these days. It's just not something most people ever really see... because most people aren't following around the folks that do stuff like fecal smears to monitor parasite loads of managed herds.<br /> <br /> Not really insightful to the mage side of things, but it at least helps calibrate what sort of existing tech is out there for appropriate mages to consider using normal tech/enhanced tech over directly using magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-28T03:41:22-08:00","id":1546463,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't paradigms be more important? Admittedly, if you're thinking &quot;microscopic vision&quot; it already tends to a scientific world view. But wouldn't a shaman seek aide from spirits to see the incredibly small?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-28T03:58:11-08:00","id":1546464,"title":"","content":"Focus doesn't change what Spheres a base effect is. Asking a spirit to let you see the world of the smallest living things is still a Forces 2 effect to magnify what you can see. Asking a spirit if the soil is healthy is still a Life 1/Matter 1 effect to understand how the intersection of living and inert parts of the soil are doing. A &quot;standard&quot; Dreamspeaker might be far more inclined towards the second option based on their magical style, but if they actually want to see the microscopic directly, they need to use magic that actually does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-28T04:42:45-08:00","id":1546465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steve Bridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546460#post1546460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would probably let someone do this with a Correspondence 2 effect, provided it falls into line with their own practices of magic. If a mage uses a telescope as a tool for Correspondence, for instance, the idea of exploiting the same concept &quot;in reverse&quot; seems fairly natural to me. A Virtual Adept who understands the world as a manifestation of information could probably justify filtering that to a much smaller scale for examination. To a Hermetic, it might simply be a matter of adjusting mathematics and symbols they use to provide this sort of focus, when making use of scrying practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Distorting proportions would be in Corespondence 4. Paradigm or practice should have nothing to do with that. Keep in mind a character may think he can do what in reality he cannot.<br /> You could use some variant of Data to make it lower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-28T07:37:27-08:00","id":1546467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546463#post1546463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't paradigms be more important? Admittedly, if you're thinking &quot;microscopic vision&quot; it already tends to a scientific world view. But wouldn't a shaman seek aide from spirits to see the incredibly small?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! That's another possibility I hadn't thought of! Aside from certain paradigms adding a bit of Spirit to any sort of magic, which M20 deals with a bit, I can easily see a Verbenna or Dreakspeaker using some sort of rote to share the perceptions of a much smaller creature for this purpose. It would be somewhat like forming a mental connection with an eagle or hawk to view the landscape from above, but instead sharing the perceptions of a mouse, or even a fly. This might add some interesting twists to it, given that sight functions somewhat differently for other lifeforms, and that may not be exactly what a practitioner of this method is accustomed to. Also, if this is done in a more cooperative manner, one's partner in the endeavor might find itself easily distracted by certain things in a manner which is in keeping with its basic nature. This might not necessarily be a disadvantage, as it might notice something which the mage otherwise wouldn't even think to look for, being more accustomed to its own perspective than the mage is. &quot;Alright, we're looking for tiny fragments of metal..&quot; &quot;Hey, this coat smells good! I think there's some crumbs in the pockets!&quot;<br /> <br /> Asking a spirit to share its perceptions with you might also be interesting, and might result in shared perceptions which are more or less than what the mage intended. Especially if a spirit is using its own abilities to grant a mage this sort of vision, that's going to be colored and nuanced in a manner particular to that spirit's perceptions of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 11-28-2024, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-28T08:24:53-08:00","id":1546469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546465#post1546465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Distorting proportions would be in Corespondence 4. Paradigm or practice should have nothing to do with that. Keep in mind a character may think he can do what in reality he cannot.<br /> You could use some variant of Data to make it lower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't rank 4 Correspondence deal more with actually distorting the relationships between objects and spaces, as opposed to altering one's own perspective? I understand that opinions on the nitty-gritty of how space and perception work depend on the paradigm of the individual mage, and whether they believe that the world is a hologram/illusion/representation of pure information/etc. (I love that M20 goes into a lot of detail on this to let players fiddle highly divergent ideas about it into the framework of even a single Tradition.)<br /> <br /> What I've managed to glean is that the first rank of Correspondence allows the user to understand the relationships between objects and spaces, but they're not yet able to shift those perceptions outside what they think of as their own personal perspective relative to their own body.<br /> <br /> At the second rank, they've realized that perception is no longer necessarily bound to their own personal location, relative to anything else they have enough of a mental &quot;hold&quot; on to make that relative to. Thus, they can choose to shift that perception 20 feet above, relative to some particular space. It's very much an &quot;I no longer need eyes to see&quot; thing. (Replace &quot;see&quot; with any other sense, if the way this is written is to be accepted.) It doesn't seem to me that matters of scale really come into it at that point, as we are in fact no longer really talking about how the human eye works, the mage having moved beyond that sort of limitation.<br /> <br /> Granted, that sort of notion is going to come more easily to certain paradigms than others, and the tools one works with are tightly bound up with paradigm, especially if you're going with M20. If a mage uses something involving lenses as a tool for Correspondence workings, the idea of shifting the scale of perception will probably come to them easily. Not necessarily so for a different mage who likes to use flames or trance states for scrying practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-28T09:44:35-08:00","id":1546470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steve Bridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546469#post1546469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't rank 4 Correspondence deal more with actually distorting the relationships between objects and spaces, as opposed to altering one's own perspective? I understand that opinions on the nitty-gritty of how space and perception work depend on the paradigm of the individual mage, and whether they believe that the world is a hologram/illusion/representation of pure information/etc. (I love that M20 goes into a lot of detail on this to let players fiddle highly divergent ideas about it into the framework of even a single Tradition.)<br /> <br /> What I've managed to glean is that the first rank of Correspondence allows the user to understand the relationships between objects and spaces, but they're not yet able to shift those perceptions outside what they think of as their own personal perspective relative to their own body.<br /> <br /> At the second rank, they've realized that perception is no longer necessarily bound to their own personal location, relative to anything else they have enough of a mental &quot;hold&quot; on to make that relative to. Thus, they can choose to shift that perception 20 feet above, relative to some particular space. It's very much an &quot;I no longer need eyes to see&quot; thing. (Replace &quot;see&quot; with any other sense, if the way this is written is to be accepted.) It doesn't seem to me that matters of scale really come into it at that point, as we are in fact no longer really talking about how the human eye works, the mage having moved beyond that sort of limitation.<br /> <br /> Granted, that sort of notion is going to come more easily to certain paradigms than others, and the tools one works with are tightly bound up with paradigm, especially if you're going with M20. If a mage uses something involving lenses as a tool for Correspondence workings, the idea of shifting the scale of perception will probably come to them easily. Not necessarily so for a different mage who likes to use flames or trance states for scrying practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradigm mostly tells you how you do something and what you cant do, not what spheres and sphere lvls you use.<br /> Spheres are a meta mechainc that have nothing to do with the fiction (part of being the paradigm for the order of hermes that is)<br /> <br /> To distort reality to the point of seeing small stuff as big or big stuff as small you need correspondence 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-28T12:53:59-08:00","id":1546474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546451#post1546451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perception effects can be skinned however is appropriate for the mage in question so as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> indicated, you have to distinguish between the effect &quot;manipulate the world to see things as if through a microscope&quot; and &quot;theme the perception effect as microscopic vision.&quot;<br /> <br /> A spell that actually works like a microscope is going to be a Forces 2 effect to manipulate the light, Life 3/4 to physically change the structure of the eye, or maybe Correspondence 3 to colocate perceptions in a clever way.<br /> <br /> A spell that is themed like a microscope is much more open and could include the Life 1/Matter 1 option. Correspondence 1 in theory should show everything in the area though I'm inclined to say that method will definitely need the Mind 1 option of processing multiple inputs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I completely missed that last when I was trying to figure this out! Landscape of the Mind is a classic rote (across three editions) which alters the scope of perception, allowing the user to perceive their surrounding environment over a large area. Anything larger than a city block requires a conjunctional effect adding in Mind 1 in order to process that much input. Perceiving a very small area would be a simple reversal of that technique, though I'd be inclined to require Mind 1 conjunctionally for purposes of filtering Correspondence sense <i>down</i> to such a level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-29T22:08:57-08:00","id":1546496,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, that's just a Corr 1 effect. Aside from Forces 2 or Life to bend light or adjusting your eyes for the fear that is. Other than that, Corr 1 is what allows you to perceive any kind of &quot;spaces&quot;. Corr 1 could allow you much much more than Forces 2 ever would, you would in fact be able to &quot;see&quot; (detect, analyze) even atoms or perhaps even smaller units, like quarks (and maybe even the &quot;strings&quot; of string theory).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-29T22:54:56-08:00","id":1546497,"title":"","content":"There's zero in the books to support that. Correspondence, esp. alone, basically allows for two types of enhanced perceptions: sensing connections between Patterns, and projecting your normal senses to other vantages. You can sense where you are in relation to the concept of space to know exactly where you are. You can project you senses around a corner. Etc. The books don't talk about Corr perceptions in anyway modifying your ability to sense inherent information about Patterns by change the scale of your senses that you couldn't sense otherwise. Sensing atomic and subatomic structures (assuming a Focus that even acknowledges subatomic reality) is a function of Matter (and maybe Forces when you get to states of inherent particle-wave duality).<br /> <br /> Otherwise Corr senses just you beats all others. Need Matter to detect poison in your drink? Nope, Corr lets you see poison molecules. Need Mind to sense people's emotions? Nope, you just need Corr to see the parts of their brain activating to tell you what they're feeling. Need Spirit to see into the Umbra? Nope, just project your senses across metaphysical space with Corr alone. Etc. etc. etc.<br /> <br /> Correspondence is already a great Sphere with a lot of utility and potency. It doesn't need to snag tricks from other Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-30T03:22:13-08:00","id":1546499,"title":"","content":"This, and also again distorting proportions is a Corr 4 effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-30T06:10:09-08:00","id":1546500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546496#post1546496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, that's just a Corr 1 effect. Aside from Forces 2 or Life to bend light or adjusting your eyes for the fear that is. Other than that, Corr 1 is what allows you to perceive any kind of &quot;spaces&quot;. Corr 1 could allow you much much more than Forces 2 ever would, you would in fact be able to &quot;see&quot; (detect, analyze) even atoms or perhaps even smaller units, like quarks (and maybe even the &quot;strings&quot; of string theory).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right! I was initially overthinking this, and missed the precedent Landscape of the Mind sets in demonstrating that Correspondence 1 effects can alter the scope of perception, though presumably still relative to the personal location of the user. (It's at Correspondence 2 that a mage gets beyond the idea of their perception necessarily being linked to the position of their own body.) It's sometimes tricky to remember that Correspondence sensing has nothing whatsoever to do with how eyes, or any other sensory organs, work. (I can imagine this being why Akashic masters are so fond of having their students perform blindfolded exercises at times, it'd be a good way to make that point.)<br /> <br /> The reason why I'd require more advanced techniques involving pattern sensing, when examining things at the molecular level or lower, is that you're getting down to examination of patterns at that point. Mages whose paradigms are wholly or partly in line with consensus would actually be examining a Life pattern when looking at DNA molecules, for instance. (This is how Progenitor rotes explain it, anyhow.) Mystic mages would presumably be looking at the same thing at that scale, though they'll interpret it differently. This has me wondering exactly how patterns are represented in the minds of mages holding those sorts of a paradigms. Would a Chorister &quot;hear&quot; that individual's personal theme? Would a Hermetic begin seeing fragments of a person's True Name (the part of it which represents the living body?) I'm not even sure how a Euthanatos would perceive that, come to think of it..<br /> <br /> I'd even consider examination on the subatomic level to necessarily involve Prime sensing, as that seems to fit the bill for what that mage would be looking at.<br /> <br /> Requiring Mind 1 (as Landscape of the Mind does when large areas are involved) might or might not be justified. Would focusing Correspondence sense down to such a small range be a mental feat requiring that? I might look at it both ways and suggest that it's necessary unless the mage is making their examination under highly controlled conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-01T04:28:50-08:00","id":1546517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546497#post1546497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's zero in the books to support that. Correspondence, esp. alone, basically allows for two types of enhanced perceptions: sensing connections between Patterns, and projecting your normal senses to other vantages. You can sense where you are in relation to the concept of space to know exactly where you are. You can project you senses around a corner. Etc. The books don't talk about Corr perceptions in anyway modifying your ability to sense inherent information about Patterns by change the scale of your senses that you couldn't sense otherwise. Sensing atomic and subatomic structures (assuming a Focus that even acknowledges subatomic reality) is a function of Matter (and maybe Forces when you get to states of inherent particle-wave duality).<br /> <br /> Otherwise Corr senses just you beats all others. Need Matter to detect poison in your drink? Nope, Corr lets you see poison molecules. Need Mind to sense people's emotions? Nope, you just need Corr to see the parts of their brain activating to tell you what they're feeling. Need Spirit to see into the Umbra? Nope, just project your senses across metaphysical space with Corr alone. Etc. etc. etc.<br /> <br /> Correspondence is already a great Sphere with a lot of utility and potency. It doesn't need to snag tricks from other Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're reading too much in here. &quot;Seeing&quot; atoms doesn't allow you to identify them - unless you also use Matter 1.<br /> <br /> You can't identify poison just by simply using microscopic vision. Yes, you would see a bunch of molecules, but you wouldn't be able to identify them.<br /> <br /> And no, that's NOT the only things that Corr can do. I think you're too attached to the M20 shortened versions of the spheres, and just forgotten the more in depth descriptions of previous editions. Corr can allow you to discriminate ALL forms of space - specifically, that's what Corr 1 does.<br /> <br /> For all of those that watched Batman the Dark Knight (which I assume is every normal person), that sonar vision that Batman has at the end of the movie in his final fight with the Joker, that's what Corr 1 can get. With that, you can basically &quot;see&quot; a cat behind a wall. You would be able to &quot;see&quot; the rats walking at the corners of your attic. (I say &quot;see&quot;, but is more &quot;sense&quot;, as if it were an entirely new sensory system). And no, you wouldn't need Life for that. With Corr 1 you could also &quot;see&quot; a concealed weapon inside a person's jacket, and you wouldn't need Matter for that either.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAlso, you can't use Corr alone for doing an electromagnetic scan of a person's brain, because you cannot use Correspondence to look inside of Patterns. You can only detect (&quot;empty&quot;) space. You could detect a needle inside a person's... Orifice... Because that's... &quot;Empty&quot; space, but you can't use Corr 1 to look at a person's heart, because that's part of a single Pattern. You can distinguish between a person and each set of clothes and objects the person is carrying, but you can't tell if his clothes are made of cotton or synthetic.<br /> <br /> Finally, Corr 1 allows you to &quot;see&quot; in 360 degrees, but also up and down, all at the same time. You can see things behind your back, you can sense underground caves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-01T07:58:26-08:00","id":1546518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546517#post1546517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're reading too much in here. &quot;Seeing&quot; atoms doesn't allow you to identify them - unless you also use Matter 1.<br /> <br /> You can't identify poison just by simply using microscopic vision. Yes, you would see a bunch of molecules, but you wouldn't be able to identify them.<br /> <br /> And no, that's NOT the only things that Corr can do. I think you're too attached to the M20 shortened versions of the spheres, and just forgotten the more in depth descriptions of previous editions. Corr can allow you to discriminate ALL forms of space - specifically, that's what Corr 1 does.<br /> <br /> For all of those that watched Batman the Dark Knight (which I assume is every normal person), that sonar vision that Batman has at the end of the movie in his final fight with the Joker, that's what Corr 1 can get. With that, you can basically &quot;see&quot; a cat behind a wall. You would be able to &quot;see&quot; the rats walking at the corners of your attic. (I say &quot;see&quot;, but is more &quot;sense&quot;, as if it were an entirely new sensory system). And no, you wouldn't need Life for that. With Corr 1 you could also &quot;see&quot; a concealed weapon inside a person's jacket, and you wouldn't need Matter for that either.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200bAlso, you can't use Corr alone for doing an electromagnetic scan of a person's brain, because you cannot use Correspondence to look inside of Patterns. You can only detect (&quot;empty&quot;) space. You could detect a needle inside a person's... Orifice... Because that's... &quot;Empty&quot; space, but you can't use Corr 1 to look at a person's heart, because that's part of a single Pattern. You can distinguish between a person and each set of clothes and objects the person is carrying, but you can't tell if his clothes are made of cotton or synthetic.<br /> <br /> Finally, Corr 1 allows you to &quot;see&quot; in 360 degrees, but also up and down, all at the same time. You can see things behind your back, you can sense underground caves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably also worth mentioning that <i>understanding </i>what is being perceived is just as important as the ability to perceive it. A mage might be able to perceive the surface of a piece of rock in highly miniscule detail, but without at least some basic understanding of geology they wouldn't be able to determine much about the likely composition of it, or even be able to say whether it's igneous, sedimentary, metamorphic, etc.. Even with Matter 1 thrown in, which would tell them definitively what it's composed of, they wouldn't be able to make any useful assumptions about where it came from or anything but the most blatantly obvious uses of the specific type.<br /> <br /> This has come up a great deal in regard to one particular character in a long running chronicle here, a Hermetic who's been trained specifically as a seer. His master is very fond of saying things like, &quot;Any initiate can learn to see beyond sight, but most miss all but the most obvious in what they're seeing.&quot; He's spent more time being trained in skills like deductive reasoning and investigative technique than magick, and at first there was a lot of &quot;wax on, wax off&quot; in his assigned exercises. &quot;Go to this address, examine the triptych on exhibition there.&quot; &quot;What am I looking for?&quot; &quot;That would be telling.&quot; He's basically become an awakened Sherlock over the course of play, and I've even had to increasingly involve a Moriarty as a foil (a Hermetic barabbus with similar skills, his master's former master in fact.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-01-2024, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-01T21:51:46-08:00","id":1546528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546517#post1546517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Seeing&quot; atoms doesn't allow you to identify them - unless you also use Matter 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do I need Matter to count protons and neutrons to figure out what element an atom is, and thus what molecule I'm looking at? I might not have the chemical structures of lots of different things memorized, but if I could see individual atoms, I could identify water from toxic elements like arsenic and lead (both would just be counting protons and neutrons), or at least some basic poisons like methanol. A Progenitor would certainly know the physical structures of more complicated organic molecules that would at least give them pause before drinking certain ones even if a few atoms here or there could mean the difference between harmless and deadly and neither should be present in normal drinking water anyway.<br /> <br /> Seems like a Science roll should be fine if necessary, not full on Matter 1, and we're talking about mages that would be trying to examine molecules in the first place, which implies having high enough ratings in Science for such things (or access to Hypercram/etc.).<br /> <br /> So, what's stopping someone from ID molecules if you let people perceive them with Correspondence?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no, that's NOT the only things that Corr can do. </div> </div> </div>Mage Revised:<br /> <br /> &quot;In and of itself, Correspondence understanding is highly abstract. A mage skilled in Correspondence can measure space, find connections between objects and move Patterns around. Combined with the other Spheres, Corresponding becomes a formidable tool indeed.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 Immediate Spatial Perceptions<br /> <br /> Basic understanding of Correspondence allows a mage to develop precise and intuitive judgments of distance or area. A simple Effect enhances the mage\u2019s awareness of space to determine exact directions and distances. The mage can cast spells to \u201cfeel out\u201d the contours of space around her, using mystical senses to determine the placement of other Patterns even beyond the normal senses. With the proper Effects, a mage can also detect warps in space or the presence of gates, sinks, wormholes and other instabilities or tears in the very fabric of perceived distance.<br /> <br /> Combined with various Pattern Spheres, the mage can determine exact sizes and distances to creatures, objects or forces. With more ephemeral Spheres, the mage could develop a rough idea of the locations of nearby thinking beings, the area of power in a Node or the direction and distance to a peculiarity or strange coincidence.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022\u2022 Correspondence Sensing \u2014 The ancient arts of scrying take many forms. The mage might use a tiny camera, a reflecting bowl, a magic mirror or any number of means. The end results are the same: The mage draws a connection between her senses and the desired location. The mage can use her normal senses there, and thus she can watch events unfold, listen in on a conversation or perform similar feats. With Time or Spirit magic, the mage can even look into other worlds or ages, although such Effects are substantially more difficult and prone to interference or unusual results.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bSeems long the longer form older editions are not something I forgot about because they agree with me. Not that Correspondence Sensing, the basic scrying spell of the game, explicitly says that it just lets you use &quot;normal sense there.&quot; The three sample Corr 1 rotes in Revised don't say anything about &quot;discriminate all forms of space&quot; as &quot;Sense Space&quot; is Correspondence 2, and Correspondence 1 is Immediate Spatial Perceptions. Landscape of the Mind does discuss going beyond normal human perceptions, and is vague in what that means, but if you go back to the definition of Immediate Spatial Perceptions, it's clear than it doesn't let you see things you can't normally see, but rather expand the area your senses can reach and have a general idea of other Patterns being around.<br /> <br /> You explicitly need Pattern Spheres to know specifics about the Patterns around you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For all of those that watched Batman the Dark Knight (which I assume is every normal person), that sonar vision that Batman has at the end of the movie in his final fight with the Joker, that's what Corr 1 can get. </div> </div> </div>As quoted from the older books, this is incorrect. The level of detail achieved in The Dark Knight would require Correspondence combined with Pattern Spheres as it determines the exact sizes and distances to creatures and objects. The Immediate Spatial Perceptions section explicitly calls out the kind of details you're talking about as not something Correspondence can achieve on its own (even at a minimum you'd need to add Mind 1 to Landscape of the Mind and then use Correspondence 2 to direct your senses to specific areas for more details, but that's not what the example from the film does).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With Corr 1 you could also &quot;see&quot; a concealed weapon inside a person's jacket, and you wouldn't need Matter for that either.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAlso, you can't use Corr alone for doing an electromagnetic scan of a person's brain, because you cannot use Correspondence to look inside of Patterns. </div> </div> </div>This is self contradictory. If you can't see inside of other Patterns, you can't see the gun inside the jacket as it's enveloped by another Pattern, just like Mind Patterns that lead to electric pulses of the brain are within a Life Pattern. Either Correspondence 1 can pierce all spaces, including the space between Mind Patterns and Life Patterns that turn into thoughts and emotions, or it can't actually discriminate between all spaces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can only detect (&quot;empty&quot;) space. </div> </div> </div>Where is this distinction ever made? That's oddly more limited than what the books say because you can sense connections as well, not just &quot;space.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could detect a needle inside a person's... Orifice... Because that's... &quot;Empty&quot; space, but you can't use Corr 1 to look at a person's heart, because that's part of a single Pattern. You can distinguish between a person and each set of clothes and objects the person is carrying, but you can't tell if his clothes are made of cotton or synthetic. </div> </div> </div>This is, again, contradictory. From the Akashics to the Virtual Adepts, Correspondence specialists don't see space in Mage's metaphysics as the empty void between matter, but the connections between patterns. Everything exists in the singular Correspondence Point, where the physical distance between all things is zero, and only the metaphysical distance of connections truly measures closeness. Your prize hand built tool is &quot;right next to you&quot; as far as Correspondence is concerned, even if it's a few cities away in the eyes of Sleepers.<br /> <br /> So the Life Pattern of a person, and the Forces Patterns they generate such as giving off heat, electromagnetic waves from neural functions, or sonic vibrations from heart muscles pumping are closely connected in metaphysical space. As such, but your stated interpretation, they should be as easy to sense as the gun in a pocket. They ceased to be one Pattern as a nature of their function within the web of connections.<br /> <br /> Your argument needs a much more coherent explanation for the lines your drawing on why your extremely broad statement about what Corr 1 can do doesn't have all of the implications I criticized it for enabling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 12-02-2024, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T08:37:24-08:00","id":1546539,"title":"","content":"I <i>would </i>allow Correspondence to let you see fine structures, akin to zooming in with a microscope; possibly even at Correspondence 1. The catch is that it would require more successes based on how much you're trying to &quot;zoom in&quot;. In particular, I would <i>not </i>require Forces to do this. And conversely, I'd also allow for a &quot;macroscopic vision&quot; Effect that lets you &quot;zoom out&quot; and get an overview of an area, letting you take in general &quot;lay of the land&quot; details. <br /> <br /> And at higher ranks, I'd allow Correspondence to let you make things grow or shrink, similar to Ant Man; or I'd allow it to cause things to stretch or compress. With enough successes, you could achieve some rather static shape changes, such as warping a coffee cup into the shape of a donut or vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T11:48:05-08:00","id":1546542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546528#post1546528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;\u2022 Immediate Spatial Perceptions<br /> <br /> Basic understanding of Correspondence allows a mage to develop precise and intuitive judgments of distance or area. A simple Effect enhances the mage\u2019s awareness of space to determine exact directions and distances. The mage can cast spells to \u201cfeel out\u201d the contours of space around her, using mystical senses to determine the placement of other Patterns even beyond the normal senses. With the proper Effects, a mage can also detect warps in space or the presence of gates, sinks, wormholes and other instabilities or tears in the very fabric of perceived distance.<br /> <br /> Combined with various Pattern Spheres, the mage can determine exact sizes and distances to creatures, objects or forces. With more ephemeral Spheres, the mage could develop a rough idea of the locations of nearby thinking beings, the area of power in a Node or the direction and distance to a peculiarity or strange coincidence.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually reads like Correspondence 1 <i>can</i> reasonably pull off the basics of Dark Knight style vision without the help of a Pattern Sphere. It may be unable to distinguish whether what it &quot;feels out&quot; is a living creature, an object, or a force without help, but for easily recognizable shapes I question how necessary that is.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T14:46:12-08:00","id":1546544,"title":"","content":"Except it can't discern those &quot;easily recognizable shapes&quot; in the first place. Again, from the same source: &quot;&quot;In and of itself, Correspondence understanding is highly abstract.&quot; Corr 1, by itself, lets you know Patterns are around you that you can't perceive with your natural senses. But this is &quot;highly abstract&quot; as you &quot;feel out the contours of space&quot; around your character.<br /> <br /> If you use Landscape of the Mind in an active construction site and don't add in Pattern Spheres, you can sense a few stories up there's a bunch of Patterns, but you can't tell if you're sensing piles of building materials, tools, or people sitting still on the floor. You can just tell there's a bunch of Patterns clustered in one part of the construction site.<br /> <br /> Perceiving the shapes that let you say, &quot;that's a person, that's a gun, those are some dogs, that's a radio actively transmitting signals&quot; etc. requires Pattern Spheres. That's what the text says very directly. I'm not sure what you are seeing that says anything different.<br /> <br /> You don't need Pattern Spheres if you use Corr 1 to see behind you to interpret what you could see otherwise if you just turned around. But once we're in &quot;beyond normal senses&quot; territory, you need Pattern Spheres to have the information to interpret in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T03:39:26-08:00","id":1546560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546544#post1546544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it can't discern those &quot;easily recognizable shapes&quot; in the first place. Again, from the same source: &quot;&quot;In and of itself, Correspondence understanding is highly abstract.&quot; Corr 1, by itself, lets you know Patterns are around you that you can't perceive with your natural senses. But this is &quot;highly abstract&quot; as you &quot;feel out the contours of space&quot; around your character.<br /> <br /> If you use Landscape of the Mind in an active construction site and don't add in Pattern Spheres, you can sense a few stories up there's a bunch of Patterns, but you can't tell if you're sensing piles of building materials, tools, or people sitting still on the floor. You can just tell there's a bunch of Patterns clustered in one part of the construction site.<br /> <br /> Perceiving the shapes that let you say, &quot;that's a person, that's a gun, those are some dogs, that's a radio actively transmitting signals&quot; etc. requires Pattern Spheres. That's what the text says very directly. I'm not sure what you are seeing that says anything different.<br /> <br /> You don't need Pattern Spheres if you use Corr 1 to see behind you to interpret what you could see otherwise if you just turned around. But once we're in &quot;beyond normal senses&quot; territory, you need Pattern Spheres to have the information to interpret in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always seen it as the ability to map the whole area, all of empty space between other patterns. So you can scan a room and deduce that this shape is a person and that shape is a printer. Like in those pokemon guess who comercial brak things. You see the shape but can only guess what it really is. <br /> Its not the same as detecting x lifeforms. Corr 1 could probably not discern a manequin from a not moving person.but could say there is a humanoid looking thing there.<br /> Still you would have to depend on your own perceptions. It does not allow for zoom in and out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T07:25:39-08:00","id":1546563,"title":"","content":"OK, so before I respond directly I'm going to point out another piece of evidence from the books:<br /> <br /> The alternative Technocratic Spheres for Correspondence is not Dimensional Science, but rather <b>Data</b>. It is not the study of &quot;space&quot; but rather the study of how things connect to each other. Putting aside the iffy implementation of Data mechanically (search this forum for plenty of discussion of that if you want), Data, like Correspondence, is not about space as Sleepers (and we the readers) think of it (aka this &quot;empty space&quot; being brought up). We are told this multiple times, over multiple editions.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> So, added in, I don't buy it. I'm citing books, I'm pointing out precise wording from the texts, and it seems like instead of any actual reasoning based on the text, I'm having to argue against vibes.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver, Ramnesis, quelsec, and Magus Maximus, for the sake of the OP trying to understand how the game works, can we please either point to direct passages in the text that support your positions (keeping in mind you guys aren't in agreement with each other so there's at least five differing interpretations flying around in this thread), or actually walk through the reasoning of how you're getting to your positions.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have always seen it as...&quot; doesn't matter. We've all played games &quot;wrong&quot; by not reading wording closely; sometimes for the better since TTRPGs aren't always written that well and we insert more intuitive rules without even realizing it.<br /> <br /> Here's what the Landscape of the Mind rote from Revised says:<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 Landscape of the Mind \u2014 One of the most basic Correspondence exercises, this Effect opens the mage\u2019s awareness to her surroundings without recourse to normal senses. With concentration and ritual, the mage can \u201cfeel\u201d or perceive a great area of space, although extreme areas are both difficult to encompass magically (requiring many successes) and difficult to process mentally (generally requiring the aid of Mind magic for anything beyond a city block in area).&quot;<br /> <br /> As I said before, this is vague, almost uselessly vague. Unlike Sense Connection and Whereami? this is gives no examples of what this is actually supposed to do for you practically. What even counts as a &quot;great space&quot; isn't even given any guidance since magical range charts in Mage are, you know, based on sympathetic connections.<br /> <br /> So, as I already did, we go back to the general description of Correspondence, and the general description of Correspondence 1... and we get a simple message from the book. Correspondence by itself is abstract and vague in what it tells you, and you add Pattern Spheres to be more specific.<br /> <br /> Now we could go back to Mage 2e, which doesn't even try to explain the line between when Correspondence alone can do something and when you need to mix in other Spheres. You have to try to figure it out from the rote examples - a spotty proposition at best - though at least 2e's Landscape of the Mind is more clear on what it's supposed to help you do. Though it only says you can sense &quot;objects&quot; not &quot;targets&quot; or &quot;Patterns&quot; in your immediate surroundings even if you can't perceive them with your normal senses. This is a better source for &quot;you can see a gun in someone's pocket, but not electric signals in their brain,&quot; because a gun is an object and energy waves aren't. But that basically means Landscape of the Mind only really helps with Matter Patterns, which while not useless leads to some pretty counter-intuitive results (probably why Revised changed things the way it did).<br /> <br /> Sorcerer's Crusade isn't much help here (it doesn't include Landscape of the Mind, and it's Sphere descriptions are even sparser than M20, as each only gets a single page).<br /> <br /> We could also scour supplements... but that hit or miss, the supplement authors tend to be heavy handed with mixing Spheres, and which to look at is a host of debates in the making. But you're not going to find much in the way of &quot;pure&quot; Correspondence effects, and a lot of mixed Rotes for doing things that a lot of people are saying Correspondence can do on it's own. Since I was just poking around Sorcerer's Crusade to check, it has a navigation spell that uses Connection 2 (Correspondence is a newer name in the lore)/Forces 1/Matter 1 to &quot;map&quot; a route through unknown terrain. SC is nice because it actually explains what each Sphere is doing in the rote. Connection ramping up to 2 is a bit iffy on making a case for itself (essentially to get over the &quot;great distances issue even if phrased very differently), but the Forces and Matter are specifically to put moving (rivers, fires, etc.) and inert (a boulder on the trail, a damaged bridge, etc.) obstacles on your mental map before they enter sensory range so you can try to avoid them without getting lost via detours. Which reminded my of one of my favorite little rotes from Hollowers Revised that's also a navigation spell that uses Corr 1/Entropy 2 to get from A to B. Corr 1 doing the sensing of the connection of A to B, and Entropy 2 making sure you're always picking a direction that maximizes your odds of getting to where you want to be... though it notes this method doesn't guarantee safety or speed, just that you stick on a true path to your destination. While I don't really want to go through my whole collection, I think the point is pretty clear that move multiple editions, the authors of the books expect Corr 1 and 2 to get comboed with Pattern Spheres for practical effects mages are going to actually use.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, we can stick with Revised, where there's at least some clarity, and the &quot;Pokemon outline game&quot; thing really doesn't apply, or we can go back to 2e and get into heated debates on what definition of object to use in the context of the text. But to me I'm not seeing any sort of case for this desire to make Correspondence 1 do things the books never specify it can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"