sure you're always picking a direction that maximizes your odds of getting to where you want to be... though it notes this method doesn't guarantee safety or speed, just that you stick on a true path to your destination. While I don't really want to go through my whole collection, I think the point is pretty clear that move multiple editions, the authors of the books expect Corr 1 and 2 to get comboed with Pattern Spheres for practical effects mages are going to actually use.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, we can stick with Revised, where there's at least some clarity, and the &quot;Pokemon outline game&quot; thing really doesn't apply, or we can go back to 2e and get into heated debates on what definition of object to use in the context of the text. But to me I'm not seeing any sort of case for this desire to make Correspondence 1 do things the books never specify it can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>We all know the books are a mess when it comes to rotes so this does not seem as a good argument.<br /> If we have time as one of the fundaments of reality then we should also have space. Corr 2 allows you to move stuff at a distance, corr 3 to teleport and corr 4 to distort proportions to &quot;get bigger&quot; or &quot;fly&quot; or to create space loops. Thats more space flavored than connection flavored. So if i can sense time with time then i can sense space with correspondence. And what does sensing space mean? sensing everything that is not occupied by something else. As per the revisited citation it is the ability to see without other senses. When i read that i wonder &quot;what sphere at 1 would be a perfect replacement tool for a blind man&quot;? The answer is Corr 1.<br /> Lets also look on awakening where Correspondence in totality is replaced by Space and it in itself at 1 arcana is able to create the effect we are talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 12-03-2024, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T11:38:01-08:00","id":1546565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546563#post1546563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dataweaver, Ramnesis, quelsec, and Magus Maximus, for the sake of the OP trying to understand how the game works, can we please either point to direct passages in the text that support your positions (keeping in mind you guys aren't in agreement with each other so there's at least five differing interpretations flying around in this thread), or actually walk through the reasoning of how you're getting to your positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, starting with what you quoted earlier:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;\u2022 Immediate Spatial Perceptions<br /> <br /> Basic understanding of Correspondence allows a mage to develop precise and intuitive judgments of distance or area. A simple Effect enhances the mage\u2019s awareness of space to determine exact directions and distances. The mage can cast spells to \u201cfeel out\u201d the contours of space around her, using mystical senses to determine the placement of other Patterns even beyond the normal senses. With the proper Effects, a mage can also detect warps in space or the presence of gates, sinks, wormholes and other instabilities or tears in the very fabric of perceived distance.<br /> <br /> Combined with various Pattern Spheres, the mage can determine exact sizes and distances to creatures, objects or forces. With more ephemeral Spheres, the mage could develop a rough idea of the locations of nearby thinking beings, the area of power in a Node or the direction and distance to a peculiarity or strange coincidence.&quot;<br /> </div> </div> </div>Given the words &quot;Combined with various Pattern Spheres&quot; I view the first paragraph as a description of what Corr 1 alone can do and the second as what it can do with help.<br /> <br /> Now 'feel out the contours of space' can be interpreted in multiple ways, and your interpretation that the mage can see the existence and placement of patterns with no information of type, shape, or other detailed information is one of them. Nevertheless, contour at least includes the possibility that Correspondence can see details like form or outline.<br /> <br /> Notably, when we look at the second paragraph the Pattern spheres don't clearly add the ability to perceive clear outlines and shapes. We can infer that as a function of distance and space, but that's not any more plausible than inferring it as a function of the of 'contours of space.' And when we look at Landscapes of the Mind:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> &quot;\u2022 Landscape of the Mind \u2014 One of the most basic Correspondence exercises, this Effect opens the mage\u2019s awareness to her surroundings without recourse to normal senses. With concentration and ritual, the mage can \u201cfeel\u201d or perceive a great area of space, although extreme areas are both difficult to encompass magically (requiring many successes) and difficult to process mentally (generally requiring the aid of Mind magic for anything beyond a city block in area).&quot; </div> </div> </div>While you are right that this is vague, we can still get some information out of it, including that it gives a mage awareness of his surroundings. That's the most obvious interpretation that we can take out of it. Coupled with the writeup of Correspondence 1 it becomes clear that the rank does indeed give a mage at least a reasonable picture of what is around him.<br /> <br /> Now I don't have access to Revised here, so I'm going to move to M20, starting with the Correspondence 1 writeup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20, Correspondence 1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basic spatial understanding allows a mage to sense things in her immediate vicinity even if she can\u2019t perceive them with her normal senses. Using that perception, she can estimate the distances between objects; intuitively find a direction (North, South, East, West); notice hidden objects or characters; and spot spatial instabilities \u2013 warps, anomalies, wormholes, etc. \u2013 especially the ones caused by other Correspondence Effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely a similar wording to Revised, though here there is the indication that Correspondence 1 can notice hidden objects and characters, which at least implies that they can tell the difference and get some information about what the hidden thing is. The examples support this.<br /> <br /> In the section on magical fighting, a mage can use a combination of sphere knowledge and a sensory effect to ignore multiple opponent penalties. Correspondence 1 is both one of the levels of sphere knowledge and one of the effects. The wording is a little funky, but the idea is that knowledge (Corr 1, Mind 1, or Time 2) allows a mage to negate the penalty with any of the three sensory effects (Corr 1, Mind 1, or Time 1). <br /> <br /> The Correspondence 1 version of Thunder Punch allows a mage to find the &quot;perfect place to hit&quot;, and this does not need another sphere.<br /> <br /> The above two imply that either Correspondence 1 delivers more than just vague information about a target. I can indeed think of other ways this could work, but only by assuming Corr 1 abilities that are even less obvious in the sphere writeup.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Marauder, Pillory, has no eyes or ears and perceives her surroundings entirely through Correspondence and Mind magic. Pillory doesn't have Matter or Life, so can't be augmenting Correspondence here. This also lends credence to the HDYDT use of Correspondence 1 to sense a way around while blinded.<br /> <br /> For all these reasons, I find it highly plausible that Correspondence 1 senses give a reasonably accurate picture of the surrounding area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T16:48:28-08:00","id":1546568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546564#post1546564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We all know the books are a mess when it comes to rotes so this does not seem as a good argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but considering how much Landscape of the Mind is being used to justify interpretations, I can't not engage with rotes on some level if I want to say why I disagree with those interpretations.<br /> <br /> If we completely ignore Rotes, we ignore Landscape of the Mind as well, which means for every edition there's nothing outside of sample rotes that lets you project your senses beyond their normal ranges at Corr 1. &quot;360 vision&quot; is a Corr 1 thing from 1e because of it being in rotes, not the general descriptor text of the Sphere or its individual levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we have time as one of the fundaments of reality then we should also have space. </div> </div> </div>We do, Mage's metaphysical definition of space is just wildly divergent from space as perceived by us the readers. Again, every edition explains this. Mage treats discrete phenomenon perception (M20 p. 68 btw) has false. An illusion. The shadows cast in Plato's cave. Mages understand the things creating the shadows - connections for Correspondence - and thus can understand and manipulate the shadows of space and distance through their source. In Mage, space is not real, it is a trick of perception that mages learn to see through.<br /> <br /> The practical applications favor &quot;space flavored&quot; as you put it because mages still operate in Consensus and Consensus believes in discrete phenomenon perception as reality. Mages use Correspondence to overcome the illusion of discrete space, so lots of their magic deals in space because that's the part of Consensus Reality they're imposing their will over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what does sensing space mean? </div> </div> </div>Sensing the connections between things (including how those connections manifest as discrete spaces within Reality).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As per the revisited citation it is the ability to see without other senses. </div> </div> </div>Sense, not see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When i read that i wonder &quot;what sphere at 1 would be a perfect replacement tool for a blind man&quot;? The answer is Corr 1. </div> </div> </div>This strikes me as very ignorant of what it's like to deal with severe visual impairment. Blind people get by without sight or magic because they still have all of their other senses and adapt.<br /> <br /> Corr 1 is never going to replace having unimpaired eyes. What it can most certainly do is aid heavily in how blind people already learn to navigate the world with the rest of their senses. My grandfather was declared legally blind in his 20s and spent almost 80 years without the ability to do things most people take for granted. But in familiar spaces, he was remarkably functional through something most visually impaired people use: order. If everything always goes back to the same place, then you don't need eyes to find it. I had this drilled into me as a kid because... kids are chaotic and disruptive. I, a fully sighted person, still have his old house mapped out in my head to the level of knowing exactly where the butter dish sat on the kitchen table, to make sure it was where it was supposed to be when he sat down for breakfast and would butter his own toast.<br /> <br /> Gaining that understanding in unfamiliar places? That's why a blind person wants Corr 1. To do in minutes what normally takes years, and not have to worry if people move stuff around on you because what's important is how everything relates to everything else and with Corr 1 you can remap on demand. Instead of having to memorize paths based on feel and even stepping and hoping nobody moved your things around, you have magic. You don't &quot;see&quot; because you're blind. The world is still &quot;so many steps from the door to the table,&quot; and &quot;if my elbow is on the edge of the table, the butter is at the tips of my outstretched fingers.&quot; Magic lets you feel the world instead of having to learn it. Which is a lot, but it's not the fantasy of Daredevil or whatever other blind-ness overcoming superpowers/magic/fantasy that most people think of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lets also look on awakening ... </div> </div> </div>Why? Different game, completely different underlying metaphysics of the magic in it.<br /> <br /> Also completely different design approaches as Ascension heavily focuses on mixing Spheres, while Awakening prefers to have each Arcanum to be independent for most use cases (creating something from nothing is just higher ranked magic instead of adding Prime for example) and relies and far more robust general magic rules to set the limits of what mages can do at their current level of power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546565#post1546565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the words &quot;Combined with various Pattern Spheres&quot; I view the first paragraph as a description of what Corr 1 alone can do and the second as what it can do with help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Notably, when we look at the second paragraph the Pattern spheres don't clearly add the ability to perceive clear outlines and shapes. We can infer that as a function of distance and space, but that's not any more plausible than inferring it as a function of the of 'contours of space.' </div> </div> </div>That skips the second paragraph saying, &quot;Combined with various Pattern Spheres, the mage can determine exact sizes and distances to creatures, objects or forces.&quot; Yes it doesn't use the words &quot;outlines&quot; or &quot;shapes,&quot; but if you need Pattern spheres to judge exact sizes, then the level of detail of Correspondence alone you're attributing doesn't make sense. And &quot;outline&quot; is an exact size, even if the details within the outline aren't perceived. The presence of that clause puts the inference on &quot;outlines and shapes&quot; under the Pattern Sphere add-ons, because it includes size, as dimensional measurement, not more specific measurements associated with other Spheres. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is definitely a similar wording to Revised, though here there is the indication that Correspondence 1 can notice hidden objects and characters, which at least implies that they can tell the difference and get some information about what the hidden thing is. The examples support this. </div> </div> </div>While I agree M20's write up is more practically minded than Revised is regarding something like &quot;you can sense hidden things,&quot; M20, like 2e, really doesn't go into where the limits of Correspondence alone are. Frustratingly M20 left zero examples under Perceptions &amp; Psychic Powers (core) or Enhanced Perceptions (HDYDT?). Reaching all the way into the combat section doesn't really help much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The above two imply that either Correspondence 1 delivers more than just vague information about a target. </div> </div> </div>Both examples have a distinct flaw for the point being made though: you can still perceive with your normal senses. Correspondence is being layered on-top of things you can already sense. If you're fighting three people, you already know that, and know generally where they are. Correspondence is helping you deal with relative positioning to avoid penalties, not letting you see things you can't see. Thunder Punch (though I find that side bar a bit weird since that's been an Entropy 1 thing since the beginning and HDYDT drops Corr from basic combat magic), is again, not sensing things beyond your normal perceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T23:46:50-08:00","id":1546579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546568#post1546568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> This strikes me as very ignorant of what it's like to deal with severe visual impairment. Blind people get by without sight or magic because they still have all of their other senses and adapt.<br /> <br /> Corr 1 is never going to replace having unimpaired eyes. What it can most certainly do is aid heavily in how blind people already learn to navigate the world with the rest of their senses. My grandfather was declared legally blind in his 20s and spent almost 80 years without the ability to do things most people take for granted. But in familiar spaces, he was remarkably functional through something most visually impaired people use: order. If everything always goes back to the same place, then you don't need eyes to find it. I had this drilled into me as a kid because... kids are chaotic and disruptive. I, a fully sighted person, still have his old house mapped out in my head to the level of knowing exactly where the butter dish sat on the kitchen table, to make sure it was where it was supposed to be when he sat down for breakfast and would butter his own toast.<br /> <br /> Gaining that understanding in unfamiliar places? That's why a blind person wants Corr 1. To do in minutes what normally takes years, and not have to worry if people move stuff around on you because what's important is how everything relates to everything else and with Corr 1 you can remap on demand. Instead of having to memorize paths based on feel and even stepping and hoping nobody moved your things around, you have magic. You don't &quot;see&quot; because you're blind. The world is still &quot;so many steps from the door to the table,&quot; and &quot;if my elbow is on the edge of the table, the butter is at the tips of my outstretched fingers.&quot; Magic lets you feel the world instead of having to learn it. Which is a lot, but it's not the fantasy of Daredevil or whatever other blind-ness overcoming superpowers/magic/fantasy that most people think of.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dont really see why it shouldnt be a superpower replacement like in daredevil, it clearly is in Awakening and the game is fine. Magic replaces/cures many defects, nothing new here. As for blindness Life can cure it in full, Forces can give you echolocation and Corr can give you the perfect orientation where everywhere is again similar to echolocation (in effect not method) or a bit better.<br /> <br /> As for the examples being in line of normal perceptions it does not matter if the sphere allows you to pinpiont things. It means it is very very precise so maping a human shape from a table shape should be easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T02:50:04-08:00","id":1546581,"title":"","content":"If you want to play Awakening, play Awakening, it's a fun game. It is not, however, Ascension, and I already pointed out why you can't directly translate what Awakening does to what Ascension does. But importantly for this? The WoD and CofD handle significant flaws very differently. In Ascension you have to take the Blind Flaw, which gives you points up front, specific mechanics, and is part of your Pattern (so removing it with Life is a lot more involved than healing damage). In Awakening you take a Persistent Blinded Condition. That only gives you Beats if it actually impairs your character (which means it isn't if you use magic to overcome it all the time), and the ST can simply remove a Condition from your sheet if it never actually comes up. Again, very different design mentalities between the games.<br /> <br /> And as for why beyond that? Because that's not what the rules actually say. If Ascension wanted it that way, it would say that's what it does.<br /> <br /> If you want to house rule it? Great! But don't conflate that with what the books say so we can actually have fruitful discussions that answer questions people pose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T03:39:42-08:00","id":1546583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546581#post1546581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to play Awakening, play Awakening, it's a fun game. It is not, however, Ascension, and I already pointed out why you can't directly translate what Awakening does to what Ascension does. But importantly for this? The WoD and CofD handle significant flaws very differently. In Ascension you have to take the Blind Flaw, which gives you points up front, specific mechanics, and is part of your Pattern (so removing it with Life is a lot more involved than healing damage). In Awakening you take a Persistent Blinded Condition. That only gives you Beats if it actually impairs your character (which means it isn't if you use magic to overcome it all the time), and the ST can simply remove a Condition from your sheet if it never actually comes up. Again, very different design mentalities between the games.<br /> <br /> And as for why beyond that? Because that's not what the rules actually say. If Ascension wanted it that way, it would say that's what it does.<br /> <br /> If you want to house rule it? Great! But don't conflate that with what the books say so we can actually have fruitful discussions that answer questions people pose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books dont point convincingly to your point either. It could be both for as far as we know. Where you see something different i see just a fancy way of saying that it can map space.<br /> Whitch at this point is not a big problem as we see inconsistencies everywhere in the books. Just dunno why you wana make coresponcence the weakest 1 lvl sphere.<br /> <br /> As for Blindnes in ascension there are dozens of methods to go around it and everybody that takes that flaw in mage goes around it with magic. Corr 1 isnt even the best option here as a few Forces 1 effects could give a more complete view. Even Matter 1 could allow the same as air is matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T04:58:58-08:00","id":1546584,"title":"","content":"If I could find a passage that says exactly what I've been saying from the books, people that don't want to be convinced still wouldn't be convinced.<br /> <br /> I'm a lot more confident my reading is closer to the text's intent because I'm not resorting to things like making up effects (Forces 1 alone, and Matter 1 alone, cannot make up for being blind), or claiming that Correspondence 1 working like what the books say level 1 Spheres should do (sense the basic subjects of the Sphere, which are connections and dimensions, not comic book x-ray vision and super-sonar) is twisting it to be weaker than other Spheres. I'm not &quot;making&quot; Correspondence 1 anything, I'm trying to make the best case for what the books mean when they say what it's capable of. If that's overly weak, that's good to know so we can house rule it to what we want it to be, if it's too powerful, same thing.<br /> <br /> That said, Time 1 is the weakest (having a perfect internal clock is the one thing Time 1 can do and no other Sphere can do at level one since Prime can also detect supernatural distortions to time by detecting the magic instead of detecting time going wonky), and the strongest is a coin flip between Mind and Entropy (Mind has more potent straight up mechanics, Entropy is looser and more subject to ST calls when it comes to actual impact but is flat out the broadest sensory effect in the game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T05:07:17-08:00","id":1546585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546584#post1546584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (Forces 1 alone, and Matter 1 alone, cannot make up for being blind),</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Where does it say it cant?<br /> <br /> Time 1 has the perfect mement that is way better than Corr1 without area maping.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T06:20:28-08:00","id":1546587,"title":"","content":"That's not how the rules are constructed. They need to say a Sphere can do something for it to do something. Forces says you can enhance your perception to see a type of Forces Pattern within the framework of your functional senses and Focus. Forces 1 lets you perceive sounds around you with superhuman efficiency, but it doesn't mean you know how to echolocate (something you could train yourself to do without magic) or magically give you a sonar-sense. Matter 1 lets you know things about objects basic material properties, so you can know you're touching wood, or stone, or glass, but it doesn't mean you get a mental image of the total object's size, function, and so on.<br /> <br /> The Perfect Moment section of HDYDT? provides examples of most of the Spheres getting to do The Perfect Moment with just their level 1. So that's not a Time specific thing (even Correspondence 1 gets a The Perfect Moment example). It's literally an example of how Time 1 really isn't that special. The Perfect Moment is also just one of dozens of ways to flavor Magic Enhancing Abilities. If you bought up Echolocation as a Secondary Skill Forces 1 doesn't need The Perfect Moment to reduce the difficulty of your echolocation rolls. The magical ability to directly sense sonic Patterns is plenty of justification for that. The Perfect Moment section actually supports something I've been getting at here: Time 1 The Perfect Moment effects are only good for simple actions that are intuitive and don't require significant understanding of the situation or subjects to get right. It goes on with all of the other Sphere examples to illustrate how more complex situations need other Spheres to get The Perfect Moment instead because the knowledge of those systems is more important. <br /> <br /> Just like The Perfect Moment, where you're supposed to use other Spheres for more detailed situation when Time alone doesn't impart enough, Correspondence 1 only tells you so much rather than blanket super-senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T08:22:19-08:00","id":1546589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546568#post1546568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That skips the second paragraph saying, &quot;Combined with various Pattern Spheres, the mage can determine exact sizes and distances to creatures, objects or forces.&quot; Yes it doesn't use the words &quot;outlines&quot; or &quot;shapes,&quot; but if you need Pattern spheres to judge exact sizes, then the level of detail of Correspondence alone you're attributing doesn't make sense. And &quot;outline&quot; is an exact size, even if the details within the outline aren't perceived. The presence of that clause puts the inference on &quot;outlines and shapes&quot; under the Pattern Sphere add-ons, because it includes size, as dimensional measurement, not more specific measurements associated with other Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I addressed that specific clause, it clearly doesn't skip it. Like I said, outlines could be a function of the second paragraphs distance and size, but they also could be a function of the first paragraphs &quot;exact directions and distance&quot; and &quot;contours of space.&quot; Indeed, it is difficult to see how those couldn't be used to make an outline map of the surrounding area.<br /> <br /> For the record, if I thought the two paragraphs actually contradicted I would suspect the problem was in the second, not the first. Not only is the first more consistent with Landscape of the Mind, but Mage does have a tendency for sphere bloat so I err on the side of simplicity. But here's an illustration of what I think is actually happening:<br /> <br /> Let's say Johnny Depp was hiding amongst the animatronics of the Pirates of the Caribbean ride (I actually don't know if that ride uses forced perspective, so for the sake of the example lets assume they are life size).<br /> <br /> Correspondence 1 can build a map of the area. It can show the humanoid figures, tell the difference between them and the rocks, and see them move. It can do this all whether the lights are on or off and regardless of which direction the mage is looking.<br /> <br /> What it cannot do is easily show the difference between the animatronics and Johnny Depp. That requires either additional spheres or context clues. With Mind, the mage could figure out the exact distance and location of the one that has a mind, with Life, he could figure out the exact distance to Depp, with Matter, he could figure out the distance of the animatronics. Without those, he's stuck using context clues. Someone sneaking up behind him probably isn't an animatronic, but even then he wouldn't know if that someone was Depp or someone else. <br /> <br /> And if Ian Malcolm was wrong and when Pirates of the Caribbean breaks down the pirates really do try to eat the tourists, the mage would only know is that a humanoid was approaching him, not what it was.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T08:27:49-08:00","id":1546590,"title":"","content":"Lets agree to dissagree.<br /> Forces 1 can do far more than you describe. For example it could decipher radiowaves into speach, compared to that echolocation is easy peasy. To train Echolocation you have to learn how sound riples from things and comes back to you. With Forces you do not have to do that. You can sense the soundwaves in thei pure form. Yes its all tied to your perceptions but nothing says mage cant get new better senses thanks to it. Termovision and radiosound receivement is just one of those.<br /> <br /> Time 1 is mentioned in the bullet catching rote. It allows you to perfectly know when the bullet will get to you. Perfectly. I can only assume other 1 lvl spheres work in similar ways. The same way Life 1 lets you scan someone for illnesses without medical knowledge. The same way Matter 1 lets you find imperfections that you cant see. The same way Prime allows you to figure out magic to counterspell it. And so on and on....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T20:00:21-08:00","id":1546620,"title":"","content":"Though it's very much off the original subject, being able to sense one sort of pattern or another is highly useful, but that usefulness depends to a certain extent on the user having enough knowledge to understand the meaning of what they're seeing. Knowing the exact material composition of the substance in a vial, for instance, doesn't reveal the fact that it's deadly to living things without some knowledge of applied chemistry or toxicology. This is why every Etherite character I've ever had in a game started with different physical science skills, and why Verbena without any practical and useful understanding of living things (represented on paper as skills) get funny looks from their peers.<br /> <br /> That said, pairing basic pattern sensing with that sort of knowledge can be hellishly effective. Life 1 can give a mage diagnostic tools which mundane paramedics and emergency room physicians would sell their souls for, when said mage actually knows what to do about what they're perceiving. In a similar sense, I've had more than one NPC discover that something an Etherite hurled at them was not actually magickal, and therefore not subject to their usual defenses against magick, even though they used Matter to very quickly locate the components they used to throw it together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-04-2024, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T06:41:52-08:00","id":1546638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546564#post1546564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We all know the books are a mess when it comes to rotes so this does not seem as a good argument.<br /> If we have time as one of the fundaments of reality then we should also have space. Corr 2 allows you to move stuff at a distance, corr 3 to teleport and corr 4 to distort proportions to &quot;get bigger&quot; or &quot;fly&quot; or to create space loops. Thats more space flavored than connection flavored. So if i can sense time with time then i can sense space with correspondence. And what does sensing space mean? sensing everything that is not occupied by something else. As per the revisited citation it is the ability to see without other senses. When i read that i wonder &quot;what sphere at 1 would be a perfect replacement tool for a blind man&quot;? The answer is Corr 1.<br /> Lets also look on awakening where Correspondence in totality is replaced by Space and it in itself at 1 arcana is able to create the effect we are talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Correspondence 1 is like the Daredevil's (the Marvel's superhero) &quot;sonar vision&quot;, or like I already mentioned, Batman's sonar vision device on The Dark Knight <br /> <br /> Just like Batman's sonar or, in the case of the Daredevil who is actually blind, you can't perceive colors because you aren't truly &quot;seeing&quot; with your eyes, but you're actually perceiving shapes. That's the Daredevil's entire gimmick by the way.<br /> <br /> If you add Forces 1 to it then you can perceive colors alright and it becomes full on &quot;normal&quot; vision. Then it becomes like Superman's &quot;X-Ray Vision&quot; that can see any women's underwear as if they were actually naked. With Forces 1 you can spy on your neighbors behind the walls as if they were not there. But with Corr 1 alone you can distinguish their shapes just fine.<br /> <br /> And of course &quot;distinguishing shapes&quot; is, like Heavy Arms said, &quot;vague&quot;. Just like Batman's sonar or Daredevil's sonar &quot;vision&quot; are also vague! For instance, just from the shapes of the people in the building, Batman couldn't initially distinguish from the doctors, who were actually the Joker's goons, from the hostages, who were dressed as clowns. Let's remember that scene, the Joker placed faked guns at the tied hands of the hostages dressed as clowns, therefore a mere Corr 1 wouldn't be able to discern the fake guns from real ones, and the user of the effect would probably assume then to be real based on the shape alone. Batman only figures out the deception after he jumps on one of the clowns and unmasks him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T07:33:36-08:00","id":1546639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546584#post1546584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I could find a passage that says exactly what I've been saying from the books, people that don't want to be convinced still wouldn't be convinced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny how it's always the ignorant ones who are oblivious to their own ignorance. And the irony on your own statement is absolutely hilarious, since you are the one that is usually dismissing things said in the books whenever they don't fit your view, and you project your own cognitive dissonance into others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm a lot more confident my reading is closer to the text's intent because I'm not resorting to things like making up effects </div> </div> </div>No, you're confident (and arrogant) in your reading because of your cognitive dissonance and personal bias. No other reasons other than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Forces 1 alone, and Matter 1 alone, cannot make up for being blind) </div> </div> </div>Except that it absolutely can. If Forces 1 allows you to &quot;see&quot; in total darkness, that's the same as seeing as a blind. Not so much for Matter 1, but Forces 1 beyond a doubt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or claiming that Correspondence 1 working like what the books say level 1 Spheres should do (sense the basic subjects of the Sphere, which are connections and dimensions, not comic book x-ray vision and super-sonar) is twisting it to be weaker than other Spheres. I'm not &quot;making&quot; Correspondence 1 anything, I'm trying to make the best case for what the books mean when they say what it's capable of. If that's overly weak, that's good to know so we can house rule it to what we want it to be, if it's too powerful, same thing. </div> </div> </div>You're houseruling it into something completely different from what the books say, while posing as the paladin of the RAW.<br /> <br /> And your biased cognitive dissonance is evident when you casually dismiss official printed routes because they don't conform to your bias. That's some very selective rules advocating you have.<br /> <br /> And the crux of the problem is that in your head you have the bias that &quot;Space&quot; in MtA is &quot;connections&quot;, and that it's all an illusion of the senses. This has been discussed in another topic with you yourself, and you have already been proven wrong multiple times, but like I said, your cognitive dissonance (and a little bit of personal arrogance) don't let you let go off of these wrong assumptions.<br /> <br /> Now, while this idea (&quot;space&quot; is an illusion, there are only &quot;connections&quot;) is a valid idea for MtA, it is NOT a metaphysical truth of the setting, being therefore just a theory that has as much merit as any other different Paradigms that don't agree with it.<br /> <br /> And the problem you have is that you're conflating game mechanics (aka Sphere descriptions) with the setting's metaphysics. But you're just too arrogant to recognize when you're wrong, so instead you have to lash out into detractors in a passive-agressive manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T21:43:46-08:00","id":1546891,"title":"","content":"I fully acknowledge that I'm <i>not </i>expressing a literal reading of the text, and I'm playing it somewhat fast and loose: I'm not even going to attempt to support my suggestions with textual references, because my goal isn't to present what the book explicitly says. Rather, my whole purpose here is to point out that the premise behind <b>Mage</b>'s Magick system is that it can do literally anything, even things the original writers never thought of. I point you to the notion of Primal Ventures, something that got added to the game (first through Primal Utility in <b>Convention Book Syndicate</b> and then later incorporated directly into Prime in \u200bThe Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick) literally a decade after the gameline's publication had originally ceased. Prime deals with Quintessence; but the notion that organized human activity could be a source of Quintessence is a <i>very </i>recent development. <br /> <br /> In the same way, I'm proposing that we shouldn't be restricting ourselves to what the text says a Sphere can do. If we come up with a concept that the original material never addressed, we should look for a best fit. In this case, the concept that seems to have been overlooked is Size. In particular, I find myself thinking of movies such as <i>Fantastic Voyage</i> and <i>The Incredible Shrinking Man</i>, as well as comic book characters like DC's Atom and Marvel's Ant-Man/Giant Man. Growth and Shrinking. And microscopic vision is part of the &quot;sense&quot; stage of size manipulation. To me, this feels very much like a &quot;manipulate dimensions&quot; thing, where by &quot;dimension&quot; I'm referring to the likes of length, width, and height rather than &quot;other Realms&quot;, the latter of which is what Dimensional Science means by the term. <br /> <br /> And while M20 didn't follow up on it, <b>Convention Book: Void Engineers</b> included not just Dimensional Science but also a <i>different </i>variation on Correspondence than the Data one presented in <b>Convention Book: NWO</b>: Void Correspondence, which dealt explicitly with distance. Correspondence isn't <i>just</i> about connections; it's also about geometry. And scaling up and down is very much a geometry thing. So Correspondence for changes of scale. <br /> <hr /><br /> With all that said, I'm not going to try to tell you how to make your case, or even what case to make. You want to explore what precisely the published materials do and do not explicitly support? That's your prerogative, and there's nothing wrong with that. But by the same token, don't try to tell me what sorts of arguments I'm supposed to make. Let's present a many different viewpoints here as we can, and let the OP decide for themself which, if any, they find valuable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T23:57:20-08:00","id":1546895,"title":"","content":"I didn't really bother replying directly to your older post because it included the &quot;higher&quot; level caveat for the superhero stuff. The books have always had things like the TARDIS being bigger on the inside as a Correspondence based effect, or letting you make Scooby-Doo sets where running into one room and running back out causes you to exist from a different room from where you started. And you didn't really seem to want to engage with a different post making the point that (however much it might not be fun and is worth considering house ruling) such spatial distortions would be necessary to get too small in sensory applications without other Spheres attached.<br /> <br /> You don't seem to care that I could make a solid case that having the internal dimensions of a coffee mug warp into a toroid should take a bit of Matter (if nothing else M20's not so popular lock on rules) but I feel like I'm making the key points to that to others more interested in such debates so it didn't seem to lack purpose.<br /> <br /> And for the last bit. I requested that people either focus on the books, or fully explain their reasoning. That's not telling anyone to do anything (&quot;can we please&quot; and all), and more so not advocating for approaching this in one manner of discussion. For the sake of presenting different view points, it's useful to present the entirety of it, not just the conclusion, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T05:14:51-08:00","id":1546899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546428-microscopic-vision?p=1546891#post1546891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully acknowledge that I'm <i>not </i>expressing a literal reading of the text, and I'm playing it somewhat fast and loose: I'm not even going to attempt to support my suggestions with textual references, because my goal isn't to present what the book explicitly says. Rather, my whole purpose here is to point out that the premise behind <b>Mage</b>'s Magick system is that it can do literally anything, even things the original writers never thought of. I point you to the notion of Primal Ventures, something that got added to the game (first through Primal Utility in <b>Convention Book Syndicate</b> and then later incorporated directly into Prime in The Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick) literally a decade after the gameline's publication had originally ceased. Prime deals with Quintessence; but the notion that organized human activity could be a source of Quintessence is a <i>very </i>recent development.<br /> <br /> In the same way, I'm proposing that we shouldn't be restricting ourselves to what the text says a Sphere can do. If we come up with a concept that the original material never addressed, we should look for a best fit. In this case, the concept that seems to have been overlooked is Size. In particular, I find myself thinking of movies such as <i>Fantastic Voyage</i> and <i>The Incredible Shrinking Man</i>, as well as comic book characters like DC's Atom and Marvel's Ant-Man/Giant Man. Growth and Shrinking. And microscopic vision is part of the &quot;sense&quot; stage of size manipulation. To me, this feels very much like a &quot;manipulate dimensions&quot; thing, where by &quot;dimension&quot; I'm referring to the likes of length, width, and height rather than &quot;other Realms&quot;, the latter of which is what Dimensional Science means by the term.<br /> <br /> And while M20 didn't follow up on it, <b>Convention Book: Void Engineers</b> included not just Dimensional Science but also a <i>different </i>variation on Correspondence than the Data one presented in <b>Convention Book: NWO</b>: Void Correspondence, which dealt explicitly with distance. Correspondence isn't <i>just</i> about connections; it's also about geometry. And scaling up and down is very much a geometry thing. So Correspondence for changes of scale. <hr /><br /> With all that said, I'm not going to try to tell you how to make your case, or even what case to make. You want to explore what precisely the published materials do and do not explicitly support? That's your prerogative, and there's nothing wrong with that. But by the same token, don't try to tell me what sorts of arguments I'm supposed to make. Let's present a many different viewpoints here as we can, and let the OP decide for themself which, if any, they find valuable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to add in the caveat that magick can <i>theoretically </i>do anything, but there are some things which one should not attempt or which will not work. I reserve that limitation for effects which would result in world-ending or massively world-altering events, based on the idea that more than one nephandus would already have attempted to destroy the world in that way, and since the characters are around to contemplate that fact it obviously failed to happen on each previous occasion. Either one or more powerful entities actively keep an eye out for such tomfoolery and immediately step in to prevent it, or consensus contains an element of self-preservation and pushes back <i>hard </i>when such stuff is attempted. (If consensus represents what the whole of humanity will and will not accept, it's reasonable to assume the vast majority of humanity would very strongly reject annihilation of the planet or species, at least by such overt and direct means.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-16-2024, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}